From d03c433cadea6a507f5958aef428cdb6c7051bd2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1vivy <1vivy@tutanota.com>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 23:58:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] oplus-fwk: bring up the OEM RenderNode animation glue
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implement the OEM async/spring animation helpers the OplusUI stack
drives from the render thread:

  * OplusAsyncAnimatorUtils view/rendernode setters.
  * OplusRenderNodeAnimator + IRtAnimationTarget spring animations,
    driven on the UI thread.

Fixes the graphics-side (G) animation regressions.

Change-Id: I9eeb531adcf6319354c5427c7171a4e67008853b
(cherry picked from commit 054d3e36ac1b9af6ba365b2c0c8db6fb7d4e5fe1)

Ledger: hardware_oplus.md Accepted Group C row 9 (054d3e36)
Stub-matrix: task-9-stub-inventory.md row K11 — consumer: OppoGallery2 UI animations (OplusRenderNodeAnimator/OplusAsyncAnimatorUtils, dex-scan); location: members on M13 classes in the boot jar
Change-Id: I89fd9589e9864af9a5d90f83b406d2c80a92adbc
